@@ -0,0 +1,84 @@
+# Privacy by Design — The Daily Grind website
+
+This document records how the site handles visitor data and the rules for changing it.
+Update it in the same change as any code that touches personal data or adds a third party.
+
+## Principles
+
+1. **Data minimization** — collect nothing we don't need for the visitor's request. No analytics,
+   advertising, fingerprinting, or session replay. The server keeps no request logs.
+2. **Privacy by default** — optional storage is off until the visitor opts in. Global Privacy
+   Control (`navigator.globalPrivacyControl`) and Do Not Track are honoured as opt-outs.
+3. **First-party only** — every asset (images, CSS, JS) is served from our own origin, so visiting
+   the site doesn't disclose a visitor's IP address, user agent, or the page they're on to anyone else.
+4. **Visitor control** — "Privacy Choices" in the footer lets visitors change consent and delete
+   everything the site stored on their device. Logging out wipes site data as well.
+5. **Defense in depth** — strict security headers keep injected or unreviewed code from running.
+
+## Data inventory
+
+| Data | Where | Purpose | Retention | Legal basis |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `dg:consent` (`{version, preferences}`) | `localStorage` | Remember the visitor's privacy choice | 180 days, only written when something is opted in | Consent |
+| `dg:*` preference values via `DailyGrindPrivacy.store` | `localStorage` when consented, memory otherwise | e.g. preferred store | Caller-specified TTL, max 180 days | Consent |
+| Session/auth cookies (account backend) | Cookies | Sign-in, checkout | Session; cleared on logout via `Clear-Site-Data` | Contract |
+
+There are no other cookies, storage keys, or network calls from the client.
+
+### Rules for feature code
+
+- Persist visitor data only through `window.DailyGrindPrivacy.store`. It enforces consent,
+  namespacing, and expiry. Don't call `localStorage`/`document.cookie` directly.
+- Check `DailyGrindPrivacy.hasConsent(category)` before any optional processing.
+- Never put personal data (email, name, order IDs) in URLs or query strings: they end up in
+  history, logs, and `Referer` headers. Use POST bodies.
+- Sensitive actions (logout, account changes) must be POST forms, never links.
+- Auth cookies must be `Secure; HttpOnly; SameSite=Lax` (or `Strict`) and scoped to `Path=/`.
+- Account pages served by the backend should send `Cache-Control: no-store`.
+
+## Third-party audit
+
+| Third party | Previous use | Data exposed | Decision |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Unsplash / imgix (`images.unsplash.com`) | Hero background image hotlinked on every page view | Visitor IP, user agent, `Referer` of the page | **Removed** — image self-hosted at `public/images/hero.jpg` (checked: no EXIF/GPS metadata) |
+| `statikk` via `pnpm dlx` | Dev/static server, fetched unpinned from npm on every start | Supply-chain risk; couldn't send most security headers; served the whole repo, including `package.json` | **Removed** — replaced by the zero-dependency `server.mjs`, which serves only `public/` |
+
+**Current third parties: none.** The site has no runtime or build dependencies.
+
+### Adding a third party
+
+1. Write down what data it receives (IP, cookies, identifiers, page context), where it's processed,
+   its retention, and whether a data processing agreement exists.
+2. Prefer self-hosting. If that's impossible, load it only after consent, with Subresource Integrity
+   (`integrity` + `crossorigin`) and the narrowest CSP source (full origin, never wildcards).
+3. Add the origin to `ALLOWED_ORIGINS` in `scripts/audit-third-parties.mjs`, the CSP in both
+   `server.mjs` and the `<meta>` fallback in `public/index.html`, and a row to the table above.
+
+Run the automated audit before every release:
+
+```sh
+npm run audit:privacy
+```
+
+It fails on any unreviewed origin, inline script/style/event handler (which would force
+`'unsafe-inline'`), `target="_blank"` without `noopener`, or password fields in GET forms.
+In the browser, `public/js/privacy.js` also logs any third-party request or CSP violation to the
+console. It deliberately sends no reports, because a blocked URL can contain personal data.
+
+## Security headers (`server.mjs`)
+
+| Header | Value | Why |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `Content-Security-Policy` | `default-src 'none'`, `'self'` only for script/style/img/font/connect, `frame-ancestors 'none'`, `form-action 'self'`, `base-uri 'none'`, Trusted Types | Blocks injected scripts, exfiltration to other origins, clickjacking, and form hijacking |
+| `Referrer-Policy` | `same-origin` | Other sites never learn which page a visitor came from |
+| `Permissions-Policy` | Camera, mic, geolocation, payment, sensors, `browsing-topics`, `interest-cohort`, etc. all `()` | Disables powerful/tracking APIs, including for embedded content |
+| `Strict-Transport-Security` | 2 years, `includeSubDomains` | Forces HTTPS so traffic can't be read or modified in transit |
+| `X-Content-Type-Options` | `nosniff` | Stops MIME-sniffing attacks |
+| `X-Frame-Options` | `DENY` | Clickjacking protection for older browsers |
+| `Cross-Origin-Opener/Embedder/Resource-Policy` | `same-origin` / `require-corp` / `same-origin` | Isolates the browsing context and stops other sites embedding our resources |
+| `X-DNS-Prefetch-Control` | `off` | No speculative DNS lookups that leak link targets |
+| `Clear-Site-Data` (on `POST /logout`) | `"cache", "cookies", "storage"` | Removes every trace of the session from the device |
+| `Cache-Control` | `no-cache` for HTML, `no-store` for errors/logout | Policies take effect immediately; nothing sensitive is cached |
+
+If the site is deployed behind a CDN or another host, configure the same headers there. The
+`<meta>` CSP/referrer tags in `index.html` are only a fallback (meta CSP can't express `frame-ancestors`).
